Package: PhysioML
Title: Leakage-Aware Machine Learning for Physiological Time Series
Version: 0.4.2
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Yusuke",
           family = "Matsui",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "mail.to.matsui@gmail.com")
Description: Provides leakage-aware, reproducible feature transforms and
    reference deep-learning workflows for
    physiological time series stored in PhysioExperiment objects. Canonical
    catch22 characteristics are computed through the official R backend, while
    ROCKET and MiniRocket transforms use guarded optional Python backends.
    Guarded optional torch and luz backends provide case-aware datasets,
    compact neural architectures, training, and prediction. Explicit contracts
    preserve case, channel, feature, normalization, backend, and model
    provenance without claiming clinical validation. Named transfer-learning
    policies, leakage-safe CORAL alignment, and immutable hash-verified
    foundation-model caches provide bounded reuse across domains.
Depends:
    R (>= 4.2),
    PhysioExperiment (>= 2.0.0)
